 become a doctor without  the proper documentation this loose end  was buried under a devastating story of  domestic abuse  so this pothole was missed by a lot of  viewers but for some reason it was too  great to ignore  Amelia's brain tumor the doctors at  grey-sloan Memorial Hospital don't have  it easy on top of living super hectic  lives they're constantly put in  life-threatening situations and let's  not forget that many times these  characters have gone from doctor to  patient when we found out that Amelia  Shepherd had a huge and severe brain  tumor we thought she was a goner for  sure but that's not how things played  out the thing is brain tumors are super  serious and we've seen time and time  again how devastating and crippling  brain surgery can be I don't know it's  me and was tumor talking about I love  you people tremendously most patients  don't walk away from a surgery without  some life-changing repercussions but  Amelia's tumor was removed like it was  no big deal  and she recovered as easily as someone  would from a common cold it just didn't  make sense  viewers couldn't help but feel like  Amelia's storyline was solely used to  stir the pot her speedy recovery was  nothing short of inconsistent Meredith  for the win Meredith has been through so  much from losing her mother best friend  half-sister and husband to drowning in a  ferry accident and so much more  Meredith's life is literally a  merry-go-round of disaster so we were  super happy for her when she won the  prestigious Harper Avery award in fact  we're so happy for her we almost  overlooked the major plot hole the show  created when they granted Meredith this  great honor the Harper Avery surgical  innovation goes to dr. Meredith Grey do  you remember when Cristina Yang was  nominated for that very same award in  season 10 well then you probably  remember the reason Richard Webber  couldn't choose her as a winner as it  turns out the former Seattle Grace  Hospital was co-owned by the 